  "shared_context": [
    {
      "content": "For an integer n>1 and a real number x, define E(n,x) = floor(n*x) - sum_{k=1}^n floor(k*x)/k.",
      "kind": "definition",
      "label": "E"
    },
    {
      "content": "For an integer n>=1, define H_n = sum_{k=1}^n 1/k.",
      "kind": "definition",
      "label": "H"
    },
    {
      "content": "For a real number x, define frac(x) = x - floor(x), so that 0 <= frac(x) < 1 and x = floor(x) + frac(x).",
      "kind": "notation",
      "label": "frac"
    }
  ],
  "strategy_summary": "Reduce the real-variable optimization to a canonical fractional part in [0,1), compare each point to the left endpoint of its n-interval, and then isolate the only hard step as a finite discrete bound on the rational grid m/n. The top interval [(n-1)/n,1) is then checked explicitly to attain the upper bound.",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-28T02:35:07.196565Z"
